smb: client: use atomic_t for mnt_cifs_flags

jira KERNEL-1507
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-6.12.0-211.49.1.el10_2
commit-author Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.org>
commit 4fc3a433c13944ee5766ec5b9bf6f1eb4d29b880
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-6.12.0-211.49.1.el10_2/4fc3a433.failed

Use atomic_t for cifs_sb_info::mnt_cifs_flags as it's currently
accessed locklessly and may be changed concurrently in mount/remount
and reconnect paths.

	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara (Red Hat) <pc@manguebit.org>
	Reviewed-by: David Howells <dhowells@redhat.com>
	Cc: linux-cifs@vger.kernel.org
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4fc3a433c13944ee5766ec5b9bf6f1eb4d29b880)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/smb/client/cifs_unicode.h
#	fs/smb/client/cifsfs.c
#	fs/smb/client/cifsglob.h
#	fs/smb/client/file.c
